course: dictionary
lesson: 8240
title: Rewrite and the re- prefix
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To rewrite something means to write it again, usually to make it better or different. «Crossing out and rewriting are a normal part of writing, not a sign of failure.» Even very good writers do this.
explain: The word is made from re- (again) and write. So rewrite means write again. Other re- words work the same way: redo means do again, and replay means play again.
explain: You can rewrite a sentence, a paragraph, a story or even a number. In maths, you might rewrite 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 as 4 × 3. The total stays the same, but the new way is simpler.
explain: Rewrite can also be a noun. A rewrite is a new version of a piece of writing. Professional authors often rewrite their work many times before it is published.
fact: Rewrite means to write something again, usually to make it better or different.
fact: The prefix re- means again, so redo, rewrite and replay all mean doing something one more time.
fact: A rewrite is a new version of a piece of writing.
fact: A sentence with two meanings, like «I saw a man on a hill with a telescope», can be fixed by rewriting it so that only one meaning is clear.
fact: Rewrite changes form in its verb endings: rewrites, rewrote, rewritten and rewriting.
exercise: «Crossing out and rewriting are a normal part of writing.» What does rewriting mean here? | Stopping writing forever | Drawing a picture to go with the words | *Writing again to improve it | Reading a book out loud
exercise: The prefix re- means again. Which word means to do something again? | submarine | misread | *redo | bicycle
exercise: Maya's teacher says, «Please rewrite this sentence in the past tense.» What must Maya do? | *Write the sentence again, changing it to the past tense | Put the sentence in a different book | Read the sentence out loud to the class | Count the words in the sentence
test: What is a rewrite? | *A new version of a piece of writing | Something you draw to decorate a page | A type of bicycle with three wheels | A word that means the opposite
test: In maths, which is a simpler way to write 3 + 3 + 3 + 3? | 3 + 4 | *4 × 3 | 3 × 3 | 3 ÷ 3
exam: Why do professional authors often rewrite their work before it is published? | Because books must be shorter than one page | Because re- means before | *Because a first draft can nearly always be improved | Because authors forget how to write the first time
